./DELTA.diff redesigns the analysis as a dataflow over the stack bytes each function has itself written: a stack read (x86 memory source, read-modify-write destination, cmp/test, pop, leave; AArch64 ld*, ldp record restore) needs every byte written by this function on every path since its last call (joins intersect, fixpoint per instruction); at every call the bytes below the stack pointer are dropped. Saved slots remain readable only through the modelled restore. Both reproducers are gate controls and refused, plus one-path-write and unwritten-read refusals and a both-path-write positive control.
