13:# 12. Stack bound: lib/stack_bound.py derives, from the linked executable's disassembly, a bound on
14:#     the Concrete-owned stack below main's entry, covering every byte addressed relative to the
15:#     stack or frame pointer (so the red zone), with external libc calls listed with their entry
17:#     Linux, a run under gdb (lib/stack_measure.py) must stay within it (the run measures the
18:#     stack pointer only). REPORT/stack.tsv. Controls: the analysis must refuse an unmodelled
19:#     stack-pointer write, an indirect call, recursion, a call to an unknown function, two depths
20:#     meeting, a stack pointer used as a value or written through a partial register, a partial
21:#     frame-pointer write, an indexed stack address, a saved frame pointer popped into another
22:#     register, a stack address taken, an overwritten return address, an AArch64 frame pointer
